# No internal planning in public surfaces

`internal-docs/` (PRDs, task plans, strategy, backlog) is **local/gitignored** and not part of the public repository.

## Do not

- Link to `internal-docs/` paths in commits, PR titles/descriptions, GitHub comments, or public markdown (`docs/`, `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, etc.).
- Use internal PRD numbers (e.g. `PRD-019`) in public docs or PR text unless that document is published on `main` under a public path.
- Paste task-plan checklists, wave numbers, or internal sync metadata into PR descriptions or commit bodies.

## Do

- Describe user-visible outcomes and release trains (`v1.3.2`, feature names) in public docs and PRs.
- Summarize intent in plain language when it helps reviewers (e.g. "operational safety hardening in v1.3.2") without pointing at internal filenames.
- Keep detailed planning, execution tasks, and roadmap drafts in `internal-docs/` only.

## Commits and PRs

English Conventional Commits. PR bodies cite public files, issues, and shipped tags — not internal planning artifacts.
